Attempt -- limit number of attempts for randomCurveP1P2
*******************************************************

Description
===========

When *note randomCurveP1P2: randomCurveP1P2, generates a random curve in
$\PP^3$ using the *note SpaceCurves: (SpaceCurves)Top, package, it is possible
the resulting curve will intersect the base loci of the projections used to
construct the curve in $\PP^1\times\PP^2$. If the curve does intersect the base
locusi it will generate a new random curve in $\PP^3$. The option Attempt
limits the number of attempts to find a curve disjoint from the base loci
before quitting. By default, Attempt is set to 1000.

See also
========

  * *note randomCurveP1P2: randomCurveP1P2, -- creates the ideal of a random
    curve in P^1xP^2

Functions with optional argument named Attempt:
===============================================

  * "randomCurveP1P2(...,Attempt=>...)"

