randomRationalCurve -- creates the ideal of a random rational curve of degree (d,e) in P^1xP^2
**********************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        randomRationalCurve(d,e,F)
        randomRationalCurve(d,e)
  * Inputs:
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, degree of curve on the $\PP^1$
        factor of $\PP^1\times\PP^2$
      * e, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, degree of curve on the $\PP^2$
        factor of $\PP^1\times\PP^2$
      * F, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, base ring
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, defining random rational curve in
        $\PP^1\times\PP^2$ of degree (d,e) over F.

Description
===========

Given two positive integers d,e and a ring F, randomRationalCurve returns the
ideal of a random curve in $\PP^1\times\PP^2$ of degree (d,e) defined over the
base ring F.

This is done by randomly generating two homogeneous polynomials of degree d and
three homogeneous polynomials of degree three in $F[s,t]$ defining maps
$\PP^1\to\PP^1$ and $\PP^1\to\PP^2$, respectively. The graph of the product of
these two maps in $\PP^1\times(\PP^1\times\PP^2)$ is computed, from which a
curve of bi-degree (d,e) in $\PP^1\times\PP^2$ over F is obtained by saturating
and then eliminating.

If no base ring is specified, the computations are performed over ZZ/101.

+-----------------------------------------+
|i1 : randomRationalCurve(2,3,QQ);        |
|                                         |
|o1 : Ideal of QQ[x   ..x   , x   ..x   ] |
|                  0,0   0,1   1,0   1,2  |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i2 : randomRationalCurve(2,3);           |
|                                         |
|               ZZ                        |
|o2 : Ideal of ---[x   ..x   , x   ..x   ]|
|              101  0,0   0,1   1,0   1,2 |
+-----------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

This creates a ring $F[x_{0,0},x_{0,1},x_{1,0},x_{1,1},x_{1,2}]$ in which the
resulting ideal is defined.

