resolveViaFatPoint -- returns a virtual resolution of a zero-dimensional scheme
*******************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        resolveViaFatPoint(I, irr, A)
  * Inputs:
      * J, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, saturated ideal corresponding
        to a zero-dimensional scheme
      * irr, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the irrelevant ideal
      * A, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, power you want to take the
        irrelevant ideal to
  * Outputs:
      * a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, virtual resolution of our ideal

Description
===========

Given a saturated ideal J of a zero-dimensional subscheme, irrelevant ideal
irr, and a tuple A, resolveViaFatPoint computes a free resolution of J
intersected with A-th power of the irrelevant ideal. See Theorem 4.1 of [BES20,
arXiv:1703.07631 (see https://arxiv.org/abs/1703.07631 )].

Below we follow example 4.7 of [BES20,arXiv:1703.07631 (see
https://arxiv.org/abs/1703.07631 )] and compute the virtual resolution of 6
points in $\PP^1\times\PP^1\times\PP^2$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : N = {1,1,2}                                                 |
|                                                                 |
|o1 = {1, 1, 2}                                                   |
|                                                                 |
|o1 : List                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : pts = 6                                                     |
|                                                                 |
|o2 = 6                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : (S, E) = productOfProjectiveSpaces N                        |
|                                                                 |
|o3 = (S, E)                                                      |
|                                                                 |
|o3 : Sequence                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : irr = intersect for n to #N-1 list (                        |
|         ideal select(gens S, i -> (degree i)#n == 1)            |
|         );                                                      |
|                                                                 |
|o4 : Ideal of S                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : I = saturate intersect for i to pts - 1 list (              |
|         P := sum for n to N#0 - 1 list ideal random({1,0,0}, S);|
|         Q := sum for n to N#1 - 1 list ideal random({0,1,0}, S);|
|         R := sum for n to N#2 - 1 list ideal random({0,0,1}, S);|
|         P + Q + R                                               |
|         );                                                      |
|                                                                 |
|o5 : Ideal of S                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : C = resolveViaFatPoint (I, irr, {2,1,0})                    |
|                                                                 |
|      1      17      34      24      6                           |
|o6 = S  <-- S   <-- S   <-- S   <-- S                            |
|                                                                 |
|     0      1       2       3       4                            |
|                                                                 |
|o6 : Complex                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : isVirtual(irr, C)                                           |
|                                                                 |
|o7 = true                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+

